  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chimuara-Nacala Power Transmission Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will support the country&apos;s economic development by strengthening the transmission infrastructure to facilitate the efficient and reliable transmission of new generation capacity envisioned to be developed in the Tete region. 

The overarching development objective is to support enhanced economic growth through increased access to reliable supply of electricity (and increase the electrification rate from 26% in 2014 to 45% by 2025 in the project area).

The specific objective is to enhance the transmission capability of the country&#x2019;s power grid to absorb incremental power generated from new power plants. The outcome of the project is the evacuation of additional energy produced by 479 MW of new power plants currently planned for development in Tete Province.</narrative>
  </description>
